  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Climate Risk Insurance-II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In 2025, Oxfam in Bangladesh, in partnership with World Food Programme (WFP) and local implementing organizations, will drive a comprehensive Climate Risk Insurance (CRI) initiative aimed at strengthening climate resilience in high -risk geographies across Bangladesh. Acting as a technical lead, Oxfam will spearhead the design and validation of a suite of new index -based insurance products, including for cyclones, drought, flash floods, and riverine floods in both the Jamuna and Padma basins. Through robust field data validation and collaboration with key local partners such as ESDO, RDRS, GUK, NDP, SDS, CNRS, FIVDB, Shushilan, and Uttaran, the project will ensure community -driven and context -specific product development. The initiative also emphasizes capacity strengthening of local Non Governmental Organisations (NGOs), Micro Finance Institutions (MFIs), and community cooperatives through training, orientation workshops, and partner handover processes. Strategic investments in CRI communications, advocacy campaigns, and public engagement, bolstered by tools such as dashboard development, voice SMS outreach to 17,000 farmers, and media engagement, will support widespread awareness and uptake. This year&apos;s intervention will also pilot a self -insurance product and foster the replication of sustainable, community -based climate risk transfer models adaptable for scale across Bangladesh&apos;s most climate -vulnerable districts.</narrative>
  </description>
